# Stage4 BASE package list — Orange Pi 4 LTS (Rockchip RK3399, arm64) LIGHT
# desktop. One atom per line; lines starting with # are
# ignored.
#
# This is the BASE (always-installed) set: kernel sources, U-Boot tooling, the
# mesh/provisioning dependencies, and a hardened base system. The lean DESKTOP
# stack is a SEPARATE list (packages-desktop.list) appended by the builder
# unconditionally (this platform has ONE role — no headless/none toggle the way
# Frite has --desktop none; see the builder header).
#
# NOTE on the RK3399 boot chain (EXPERIMENTAL — see specs-orangepi4-lts/README.md):
#   * Boots via mainline U-Boot (orangepi-rk3399_defconfig) and needs NO
#     proprietary blob: mainline U-Boot's TPL initialises RK3399 DRAM natively
#     (drivers/ram/rockchip/sdram_rk3399.c) and mainline ARM Trusted Firmware
#     carries a real rk3399 BL31 port (plat/rockchip/rk3399) — both confirmed
#     present upstream. This is the OPPOSITE of the RK3588 boards this list was
#     forked from, which do need Rockchip's rkbin blobs. U-Boot's distro-boot
#     then scans the first partition for /extlinux/extlinux.conf, same mechanism
#     as Frite. There is NO raspberrypi-firmware blob and NO config.txt.
#   * The board-specific DTB ships from the KERNEL build (gentoo-sources /
#     mainline), NOT from a vendor firmware package — see the builder's
#     "DTB" section. This builder does not compile U-Boot itself; the binary is
#     fetched via --uboot-url or supplied by the operator.

# ── Kernel sources (mainline; the Orange Pi RK3399 device tree is upstream) ────
# Mainline carries exactly ONE Orange Pi RK3399 device tree,
# rk3399-orangepi.dtb, and no "-4-lts" variant (confirmed by direct fetch of the
# upstream arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile). Unlike the RK3588 fork there
# is no 6.13+ HDMI floor here — the RK3399 display stack has been mainline for
# years.
sys-kernel/gentoo-sources
sys-kernel/linux-firmware

# ── Bootloader tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# u-boot-tools provides mkimage (FIT/extlinux) used to assemble the boot blob;
# the actual U-Boot binary for the board is built/fetched by the builder (see
# --uboot-url; needs Rockchip's rkbin DDR-init + TF-A BL31 blobs to be
# flashable — mainline U-Boot alone is not, mirroring Frite's Amlogic FIP/BL31
# situation).
dev-embedded/u-boot-tools

# ── Board hardware / storage ──────────────────────────────────────
sys-block/parted
sys-apps/usbutils
sys-apps/i2c-tools
sys-apps/util-linux
sys-fs/e2fsprogs
sys-fs/dosfstools
sys-apps/pciutils

# ── Networking ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
net-misc/networkmanager
net-misc/openssh
net-firewall/iptables
net-misc/socat
# Egress VPN (split-tunnel, fail-closed) — wg-quick (WireGuard, first-class) +
# openvpn (fallback) for the node-level hugmesh-egress-vpn OpenRC service
# (DEFAULT-OFF; same plumbing as every other client image).
net-vpn/wireguard-tools
net-vpn/openvpn
# WiFi supplicant is present for the onboard brcmfmac radio, which the mainline
# device tree this image boots DOES describe and enable. WiFi is still OFF BY
# DEFAULT purely for the fleet-wide hardened posture, not because of a driver
# gap (contrast the Orange Pi 5). Ethernet + the tailnet remain the primary
# path; onboard gigabit ethernet works via the SoC GMAC on this board.
net-wireless/wpa_supplicant

# ── System ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
app-admin/sudo
sys-process/cronie
sys-apps/haveged
app-editors/nano
app-misc/screen
app-misc/jq

# ── Hardened / security (SELinux LSM) ──────────────────────────────
# Same posture as the cluster images: SELinux is the LSM. The policy packages'
# pkg_postinst runs the TARGET `semodule`, which can't execute under an aarch64
# cross-emerge — so the base policy is LOADED AT FIRST BOOT (native) by
# keys-provision (shared engine). See docs/SECURITY.md.
sec-policy/selinux-base
sec-policy/selinux-base-policy
sys-apps/policycoreutils
sys-apps/semodule-utils
sys-apps/checkpolicy
sys-libs/libselinux
sys-libs/libseccomp
sys-process/audit

# NOTE: sys-fs/cryptsetup is NOT listed here — it is appended by the builder
# ONLY when --encrypt-root is set (mirrors specs-frite/portage/packages.list's
# equivalent comment); install-orangepi4-lts.sh is what actually runs
# luksFormat/open/close on the target hardware at install time.

# ── KEYS USB provisioning + attached storage ──────────────────────
# Same first-boot provisioning engine as every other client image: jq parses the
# manifests, dosfstools/util-linux handle the FAT32 KEYS partition + blkid.
net-fs/nfs-utils
net-fs/cifs-utils

# NOTE: headscale + tailscale are NOT emerged here. They are installed as
# upstream static arm64 binaries by build-orangepi4-lts-stage4.sh (the "mesh"
# phase), identical to the Frite/RPi5 images. See --skip-mesh / --skip-tailscale.
